diff --git a/libarchive/archive_write_disk.3 b/libarchive/archive_write_disk.3
index b046168..1c6878d 100644
--- a/libarchive/archive_write_disk.3
+++ b/libarchive/archive_write_disk.3
@@ -192,6 +192,32 @@ or
 .Xr getextattr 8
 .Pq FreeBSD
 for more information on extended file attributes.
+.It Cm ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_WINDOWS_SYMLINK_TYPE
+On native Windows, defer symbolic links without an explicit target type until
+.Fn archive_write_close
+so that targets extracted later can determine whether they are file or directory
+links.
+The original target text is preserved and each link is created only once.
+Explicit target types remain authoritative.
+If a target remains missing, native symlink creation uses the existing
+undefined-type heuristic; an archive cannot identify the target type of an
+otherwise unspecified dangling link.
+Extraction through a pending link, or replacing a parent of a pending entry
+with a non-directory, fails rather than changing extraction order semantics.
+Callers must check the return value of
+.Fn archive_write_close
+because link creation can fail there.
+.It Cm ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_WINDOWS_SYMLINK_FALLBACK
+On native Windows, if symbolic link creation fails for lack of privilege,
+defer materialization until
+.Fn archive_write_close .
+Directories use junctions, and files use hardlinks or copies.
+Only relative targets within the extraction root are eligible, and missing
+targets cause a close error.
+This option is independent of
+.Cm ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_WINDOWS_SYMLINK_TYPE .
+Junctions contain absolute targets and do not preserve the relocation behavior
+of relative symbolic links.
 .El
 .It Xo
 .Fn archive_write_disk_set_group_lookup ,
